      "recap_tekst": "Argentina beat Jordan 3-1.\nGoals: Jordan — Altamari (55); Argentina — Lo Celso (19), Lautaro Martinez (31) and Messi (80).\n\nLegendary No10 scores his sixth goal of World Cup 2026 as defending champions round off group stage with 3-1 victory over Jordan.\nLionel Messi came off the bench to score his sixth goal of the FIFA World Cup 2026™ as Argentina beat Jordan 3-1 in Dallas.\nHe lashed home an 80th-minute free-kick to net for the seventh successive World Cup game, setting a new record.\nWith top spot already confirmed ahead of the match, Messi was named among the substitutes as Lionel Scaloni made nine changes from the team that started their 2-0 win over Austria on Monday.\nKey stat: Argentina fielded World Cup starting XI without Lionel Messi for the first time since 30 June 2006, when La Albiceleste were beaten in a quarter-final by host nation Germany",
